{"id":"CVE-2019-10160","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2019-06-07T17:50:33.000Z","updated":"2026-10-14T06:49:52.193Z","description":"A security regression of CVE-2019-9636 was discovered in python since commit d537ab0ff9767ef024f26246899728f0116b1ec3 affecting versions 2.7, 3.5, 3.6, 3.7 and from v3.8.0a4 through v3.8.0b1, which still allows an attacker to exploit CVE-2019-9636 by abusing the user and password parts of a URL. When an application parses user-supplied URLs to store cookies, authentication credentials, or other kind of information, it is possible for an attacker to provide specially crafted URLs to make the application locate host-related information (e.g. cookies, authentication data) and send them to a different host than where it should, unlike if the URLs had been correctly parsed. The result of an attack may vary based on the application.","cwe":["CWE-172 CWE-172"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Python","product":"python","versions":["affected affects 2.7, 3.5, 3.6, 3.7, >= v3.8.0a4 and < v3.8.0b1"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://python-security.readthedocs.io/vuln/urlsplit-nfkc-normalization2.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2019-10160","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/8d0ef0b5edeae52960c7e